From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:45:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 132/342] media: a format made again for a known description is
 the known one

FormatManager::MakeFormatFor() gave every call a new encoding, also for a
description some add-on had made a format for already: a second decoder for
FFmpeg's formats (the S905's) got an encoding the readers' streams never
carry, so it never matched them. It now gets the existing format.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/kits/media/FormatManager.cpp | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/kits/media/FormatManager.cpp b/src/kits/media/FormatManager.cpp
index 12a72c21bd..f139197e51 100644
--- a/src/kits/media/FormatManager.cpp
+++ b/src/kits/media/FormatManager.cpp
@@ -192,6 +192,19 @@ FormatManager::MakeFormatFor(const media_format_description* descriptions,
 {
 	BAutolock locker(fLock);
 
+	// A description someone made a format for already (a second decoder
+	// for FFmpeg's formats, for one) gets that format: the readers' streams
+	// carry its encoding, which the second decoder's format has to match.
+	for (int32 i = 0; i < descriptionCount; i++) {
+		meta_format other(descriptions[i]);
+		const meta_format* existing = fList.BinarySearch(other,
+			meta_format::CompareDescriptions);
+		if (existing != NULL && existing->format.type == format.type) {
+			format = existing->format;
+			return B_OK;
+		}
+	}
+
 	int codec = fNextCodecID;
 	switch (format.type) {
 		case B_MEDIA_RAW_AUDIO:
